{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head d880e599fdec8ad893b15c355dfed885953d1450, tree ce9be9734e846d2d6eb7134d791dcedf349ce896, on builder/ls5-owned-room-tables-20261115, all 15 artifacts, for request 52274505 under my promise 67e40df9. This verdict names both implementations: LS-5 (request 83826277, promise fd463436, report d17e6a6e, the LS-5 note, primary) and LC-4 (request 7c37e2fd, promise 66689b08, report 56eecd58, the LC-1 note). Main 7a6fcadf is an ancestor and has not moved.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- LS-5, `packages/scope/src/room-format.ts`. `classifyRoomFormat` keeps its one catalog read, its result shape, its numeric checks and its bounded word read. Only the first `EXISTS` changes: it now counts a table only when its name is in `ROOM_TABLES`, a closed list of 66 names that earlier Scope and MCP room schemas owned. Host tables, such as the KV backing table that celld v0.6.3 creates before the constructor, no longer make unused storage read as a retired room. ScopeObject and McpAgent call the same classifier, and no SQL read is added.\n- LS-5, the Security case in `scripts/security-entry-points.test.mjs` and `scripts/fixtures/room-format-table-history.json`. The case reads the one `ROOM_TABLES` declaration and refuses a computed name or a spread. It derives the current table names from every CREATE site in the 17 schema sources, and it refuses a computed, concatenated or unsupported CREATE. It requires the list to equal the current names plus the 66 historical names exactly. A new table that is missing from the list fails this case, and so does an uppercase name.\n- LS-5, the cases. `packages/scope/test/worker.ts` seeds storage before the real constructor and observes the SQL calls without replacing any result. Earlier proxy layers now forward unchanged, so only the latest start counts. A host marker alone lets a real room create, roll back, retry and restart. An earlier `meta` table keeps a room retired, with no writes, across an eviction. An earlier `agent` table keeps a hosted agent retired, with no initialization.\n- LC-4. The two packets equal the planner's signing act 1f3b7e76 byte for byte: Lending 0.4.0 blob a69cbc3a (2,508,522 bytes, SHA-256 4692366a…) and Counter 0.4.0 blob b7e8f1b8. Their manifests carry the semantic and presentation identifiers of the committed `release-identifiers.json` at this head. `APPLICATION_TRUST` holds three rows with the same publisher and host: Lending 0.3.0 (51f8afe2), Lending 0.4.0 (1a5128d4) and Counter 0.4.0 (e8f8471e). The Counter 0.3.0 row and packet are gone, as request 7c37e2fd asks. The reproduction test requires one committed packet for each trust row and compares current source only for the authored version. That keeps the LC-1 and LC-2 rule that planner act 2d5f5930 confirmed. `scripts/format-json.mjs` and its test name the new packet paths.\n- Both notes. They keep both INCONCLUSIVE control attempts, the two test-only repairs, the planner's Linux run and the 404 probe condition of correction 65ec5705.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. The 15 artifacts name this head, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 7a6fcadf d880e599`. From the gated head 1454bd88 and from the Linux-green head dad17fde, only the two notes change.\n- Gate, END 24537e4f. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-16-ls5-lc4-gate-attempt1/gate.log` has SHA-256 f1fb52e2…, and `gate.result.json` has 59713013… with status `passed`. The log names head 1454bd88 and tree 75226586 with 0 changed files. The pins stage passed in 17.2 seconds. Kernel, Node 206, Counting 56, Plain 4890 with 1 skipped and Native 1155 with 2 skipped passed, and the last line is \"gate passed\". Scale moved into Native through `packages/scope/test/worker.ts`.\n- Controls. Attempt 3 at dad17fde: `result.json` records `passed`, the meta control DISTINGUISHES with the direct retired assertion, and the LC-4 missing-packet control DISTINGUISHES. Attempts 1 and 2 stay INCONCLUSIVE in the note.\n- Linux. Planner run 43806153520 passed at dad17fde. This head differs from dad17fde only under `notes/`, which meets the planner's condition in a26cd1d7.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 6 checked, 0 flagged. `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The fix changes one predicate inside the existing classifier and keeps the classifier's one read and its fail-closed results. Room ownership becomes a positive list, so the classifier needs no blacklist of host tables, which a host could change. The Security case keeps the list equal to the schema sources. LC-4 follows the LC-2 form and adds no new rule for historical packets.\n\nSecurity: no blocking finding.\n\n- The list decides whether storage is a retired room. A name that is missing from it would let a room that only ever had that table initialize again over old storage. The Security case closes this for current and future schemas. The 66 historical names rest on the builder's source audit of the Scope range from 59c019ef and the MCP range from a866c9aa, through 5784e23d. I read the method and the fixture, and I did not repeat that audit.\n- The note states the remaining limit: storage whose room-owned tables were all erased from outside reads as unused. The classifier cannot see history that is gone.\n- A name that a host creates and that matches the list fails toward `retired`, which is the safe direction.\n- LC-4 widens what dap-lending trusts by two releases that the planner signed with the existing publisher key. Each row has a committed packet that verifies under it. The uninstalled Counter 0.3.0 leaves the trust.\n- The deployment changes the Worker bundles. Before and after it, the planner probes one retired room on each of dap-grow, dap-lending and dap-demo, and each probe must answer 404 `not-found`.\n\nSimplification: no required change. The observer repair in `worker.ts` adds the same one-line guard to both proxies, and no assertion changes.\n\nQualifications that stand: control attempts 1 and 2 are INCONCLUSIVE, and the cause of the first timeout is unproved. Both repairs touch only the TEST Worker. The historical name list rests on a source audit. No deployment, hosted probe, new-room install or signing result follows. This approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing, before the fifth amendment of the act environment note.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d17e6a6ed46fd76cbcbd633296cfc5cab593135b","binding":"assigned","head":"d880e599fdec8ad893b15c355dfed885953d1450","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:67e40df918b7723fc65e58969ed58fa92737f6e7\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fd4634360fde9db96fba2a2e379175f68bc77c7d\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:66689b08431ea3baf27f426f86b4db0a29704e25\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:47057c8d5840cc0424eaa2d7efc2ee79585da76b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}